1
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,946
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

2
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:34,367
Look at her.

3
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:37,203
How's she not hot in that?

4
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:40,081
I hear she's a germophobe.

5
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:43,084
Her phone case is a fucking brick.

6
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:45,086
She wraps it like that 'cause of germs.

7
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:46,212
Class is starting.

8
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:48,048
Back to your seats.

9
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:51,217
If the class president says so.

10
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,391
There was a time

11
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:01,102
when I had hope.

12
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:03,438
Hey, did you just hear that?

13
00:01:03,521 --> 00:01:05,398
The class president's looking out for you.

14
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:08,568
How was that looking out for me?

15
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:16,367
So you and I can eat together.

16
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:20,663
Good Eats has the new jjajang tteokbokki.
I wanna try it.

17
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:22,791
Maybe not Good Eats…

18
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:25,335
What was that?

19
00:01:26,753 --> 00:01:27,587
What?

20
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:31,549
Your face lit up
when you saw the class president just now.

21
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:33,051
No, it didn't.

22
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:34,385
Yeah, it did.

23
00:01:37,847 --> 00:01:39,349
All right. Focus.

24
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:41,476
The hope that maybe someone out there

25
00:01:42,435 --> 00:01:45,063
could accept a monster like me.

26
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:48,149
We'll look at the average rate of change
from a to b.

27
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:53,738
Now, delta y over delta x
equals f(b) minus f(a) over b minus a…

28
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:57,826
It's Pepero Day.

29
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:00,286
I got you something too.

30
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:01,955
Thank you.

31
00:02:02,038 --> 00:02:03,206
I'll enjoy it.

32
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:10,380
I'm sorry!

33
00:02:11,047 --> 00:02:12,215
-I--
-What did you do?

34
00:02:13,341 --> 00:02:14,676
Did you get hurt?

35
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:16,052
Let me see.

36
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,262
Hey, it's bad.

37
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,764
-Was that on purpose?
-You need a doctor.

38
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:22,851
-What did she do?
-You should see a doctor.

39
00:02:23,768 --> 00:02:25,353
Are you sure you're okay?

40
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:27,230
-I'm sorry. Are you--
-Don't touch me.

41
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:29,691
Don't come near me.

42
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:39,993
But reality

43
00:02:41,619 --> 00:02:45,248
kept crushing every hope I had.

44
00:02:51,337 --> 00:02:54,174
Always telling me
I was different from everyone else.

45
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:55,175
No.

46
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,343
That I was wrong.

47
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:54,609
Sir, you should get that treated first.

48
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:56,486
It's fine.

49
00:03:56,569 --> 00:04:00,281
Check the next flight
and see if the airport's back to normal.

50
00:04:00,865 --> 00:04:01,824
Sir.

51
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:38,903
I'm sorry.

52
00:04:38,987 --> 00:04:41,531
You missed your flight because of me.

53
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,825
You were trying to protect me…

54
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,246
What's that? Are you hurt?

55
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:50,123
No, it's fine.

56
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:53,960
-Let me see. You're bleeding. Right here--
-I said it's fine.

57
00:04:55,753 --> 00:04:59,173
Now even Mr. Baek Ho-rang knows.

58
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:02,385
That I'm a monster.

59
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:07,557
You got hurt because of me.

60
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:09,684
I'm sorry.

61
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:14,981
Don't worry about it.

62
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:38,713
Why did I dare to hope again?

63
00:05:40,214 --> 00:05:41,966
Nothing about me has changed.

64
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:45,762
Why did I let myself…

65
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:50,558
hope for an ordinary life again?

66
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:13,456
Oh, wait.

67
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:36,562
What happened here?

68
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:40,149
I had it done before the trip.

69
00:06:40,733 --> 00:06:44,028
I promised I'd renovate it for you.

70
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:46,697
This place was empty, so…

71
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,243
Just

72
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:52,954
use it as a studio.

73
00:06:54,872 --> 00:06:56,249
What about the bed?

74
00:06:56,332 --> 00:06:57,166
What?

75
00:06:57,250 --> 00:07:00,169
Why did you take the bed out?

76
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:01,963
Well,

77
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:05,133
they say it's better

78
00:07:05,216 --> 00:07:08,177
to keep your workspace
and bedroom separate.

79
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:13,141
And there are plenty of spare rooms here.

80
00:07:13,224 --> 00:07:16,769
I think it'd be best to use this room
just as a workspace.

81
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:18,896
I'll just stay here.

82
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:21,399
I can sleep on the couch.

83
00:07:22,191 --> 00:07:23,317
Why?

84
00:07:24,402 --> 00:07:26,028
You don't want to come inside?

85
00:07:27,947 --> 00:07:30,366
This is a contractual relationship.

86
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:34,871
We just have to stay within ten meters.
We don't need to be any closer.

87
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:37,123
That's what you said.

88
00:07:45,506 --> 00:07:46,799
Well,

89
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:49,510
if it's because of this injury--

90
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,762
No, it's not that. It's just…

91
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:58,102
I've been thinking
about what you said in Jeju,

92
00:07:58,186 --> 00:08:00,146
and it made me a little uncomfortable.

93
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:06,486
Could you leave now? I'm a little tired.

94
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:04,377
What are you even talking about?

95
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,753
Good morning.

96
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:10,508
Hello.

97
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:24,105
Did everyone get some rest?

98
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:27,608
-Ms. Yang.
-Yes?

99
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:29,569
Can you check Mr. Baek's schedule for me?

100
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:30,486
Sure.

101
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:37,660
Did you leak Na Bo-bae's info?

102
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:57,388
RÉSUMÉ

103
00:09:58,264 --> 00:10:00,224
LOOKS LIKE SHE LIVES SOMEWHERE ELSE

104
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:01,559
Interesting.

105
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:05,646
Just let it slip
that she works at TS Resort.

106
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:08,649
Those who can't resist
digging into other people's lives

107
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:11,027
will find the rest.

108
00:10:11,527 --> 00:10:14,905
You guys know where this is?
TS Resort, the best resort in the country.

109
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:16,616
I'm here to meet Ji Eun-ho's fiancée.

110
00:10:16,699 --> 00:10:18,743
Look! It's the resort staff!

111
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:21,746
They refuse to acknowledge us.

112
00:10:21,829 --> 00:10:24,290
The fans are up in arms,
and it's total chaos!

113
00:10:24,373 --> 00:10:27,418
They're losing it, calling it favoritism.
You see this?

114
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:28,669
Man, this is…

115
00:10:30,671 --> 00:10:31,505
Yes?

116
00:10:37,261 --> 00:10:41,098
I'll head home on my own starting today.

117
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,811
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

118
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:46,854
Wait!

119
00:10:51,859 --> 00:10:53,861
What are you doing? Someone might see us.

120
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:57,907
-We said we'd only meet to charge you.
-Let's go home together.

121
00:10:58,699 --> 00:11:00,201
It's not safe to be alone now.

122
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:06,248
Did you forget?

123
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:08,793
I'm the most dangerous person.

124
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:14,298
And I'm uncomfortable
being around you all the time now.

125
00:11:24,517 --> 00:11:29,480
All right, everyone.
Let's see what TS Resort has to say.

126
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:30,648
There's a car coming!

127
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:33,859
Is that Ms. Na? Hey! Over here!

128
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:34,902
She's in there!

129
00:11:34,985 --> 00:11:37,697
Hey, these TS guys are hitting me!

130
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,365
They're hitting me!

131
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:42,118
That hurts!

132
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:53,671
Are you okay?

133
00:11:57,967 --> 00:12:00,845
Are they reporters?
They don't look like Ji Eun-ho's fans.

134
00:12:00,928 --> 00:12:02,513
They're clickbait YouTubers.

135
00:12:03,013 --> 00:12:05,850
They somehow found out
that Ms. Na works at the resort.

136
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,810
They keep showing up.

137
00:12:07,893 --> 00:12:08,936
YouTubers?

138
00:12:09,603 --> 00:12:12,565
Are you saying they're all here
to catch Ms. Na on camera?

139
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:16,444
She said she'd go home alone today.

140
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:18,195
I saw her leave through the back door.

141
00:12:18,779 --> 00:12:20,573
Don't worry, I assigned her a bodyguard.

142
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:22,158
Oh, really?

143
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,161
For now,

144
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:28,164
tighten security at the resort.

145
00:12:28,664 --> 00:12:32,543
Report them all
for obstruction of business.

146
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:35,421
Don't let them lay a finger on Ms. Na.

147
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:37,548
Yes, sir.

148
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,103
15 NEW MESSAGES FROM SEO-JEONG

149
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:52,855
9 NEW MESSAGES FROM PRECIOUS

150
00:12:56,776 --> 00:12:59,195
Bo-bae, why aren't you picking up?

151
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:01,572
We're always on your side, okay?

152
00:13:01,655 --> 00:13:03,491
Na Bo-bae, aren't you going to reply?

153
00:13:03,574 --> 00:13:04,533
Are you okay?

154
00:13:04,617 --> 00:13:06,327
Call me as soon as you see this.

155
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,996
What am I supposed to tell
Ji-hye and Yong-gi?

156
00:13:14,418 --> 00:13:15,544
JU-HEE

157
00:13:15,628 --> 00:13:17,713
Bo-bae, are you okay?

158
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:22,134
This is about you, right? This is awful.

159
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:25,596
I know you're laughing
while sending crying emojis.

160
00:13:31,393 --> 00:13:33,270
THE WOMAN JI EUN-HO PROPOSED TO
IS A DRAMA WRITER

161
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,398
She's only written a one-act.

162
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:38,609
-Na Bo-who?
-A writer? Yeah, right.

163
00:13:38,692 --> 00:13:41,278
-Anybody's a writer now.
-She wrote Eun-ho's debut?

164
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:42,196
She got him then.

165
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:44,657
-Wistful Youth?
-Focus on your writing.

166
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:46,450
Failed as a writer, chased an actor.

167
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:49,328
She's not even that pretty.
What's with her hair?

168
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:50,663
-Her hair's a mess.
-Crazy.

169
00:13:50,746 --> 00:13:51,580
Unbelievable.

170
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,123
She doesn't know her place.

171
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:54,667
Like they know anything.

172
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:57,378
Maybe I should just sue them all.

173
00:14:00,214 --> 00:14:02,675
It's not true. Why can't I say so?

174
00:14:02,758 --> 00:14:04,009
Bo-bae…

175
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,095
What about Ms. Na's reputation?

176
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:08,389
This is on me. I should explain.

177
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:10,432
Type "Ji Eun-ho" into the search bar,

178
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:12,268
and "Na Bo-bae" comes up beside it.

179
00:14:13,018 --> 00:14:15,604
You look like some idiot
who's lost his head over a woman.

180
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:17,356
She's getting it worse than I am.

181
00:14:17,439 --> 00:14:19,817
Right now,
all over social media and the news--

182
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,277
Exactly!

183
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:23,863
You're a celebrity, Eun-ho.

184
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:26,782
The moment you try to explain this rumor,

185
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:29,743
you add fuel to a fire
that could've died down on its own.

186
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:32,037
Then what's going to happen to her?

187
00:14:34,248 --> 00:14:36,584
The best thing you can do is say nothing.

188
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:39,628
The fastest way for this to blow over
is to keep your mouth shut.

189
00:14:53,851 --> 00:14:56,979
Find out who started the rumor
about Ms. Na and Ji Eun-ho.

190
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:58,147
Sorry?

191
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:00,316
We need to put this rumor to rest.

192
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,903
One's the face of TS Resort,
and the other…

193
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:08,449
is my secretary.

194
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:11,785
Sir, is this really the time for that?

195
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:13,704
The TS Hotel embezzlement case…

196
00:15:16,415 --> 00:15:17,625
It's time to expose it.

197
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:19,627
The situation has changed.

198
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:22,129
When the situation changes,
so does the plan.

199
00:15:30,554 --> 00:15:32,222
Hello.

200
00:15:33,098 --> 00:15:34,642
-Hello.
-Good to see you.

201
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:36,268
Thank you for coming all this way.

202
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:37,186
-Pleasure.
-Yes.

203
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,659
Mr. Yoon.

204
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:54,536
We've done well for the past 15 years.

205
00:15:55,037 --> 00:15:55,913
Right?

206
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:59,583
Yes. We have.

207
00:16:01,543 --> 00:16:03,212
You may feel a little uneasy

208
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:06,757
since it looks like
you're taking the fall alone,

209
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:10,886
but you've benefited from it
all these years too.

210
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:15,349
Just do a little time…

211
00:16:17,518 --> 00:16:20,938
and I'll make sure
your daughter is set for life.

212
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:31,991
Yes.

213
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:33,409
Yes, sir.

214
00:16:35,327 --> 00:16:36,662
Oh man.

215
00:16:37,621 --> 00:16:41,000
I can't wait to see
the look on Ho-rang's face.

216
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:48,716
I wonder how he'll react
when the article comes out.

217
00:16:51,135 --> 00:16:54,972
Why did you ask us to come here?

218
00:16:55,055 --> 00:16:56,390
I'd like to know too.

219
00:16:56,473 --> 00:16:58,100
Why would you need

220
00:16:58,183 --> 00:17:00,686
a failing newspaper publisher
and a TV broadcaster?

221
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:04,773
Come on. Don't be so modest.

222
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:09,361
You two have the country's press and media
in the palm of your hand.

223
00:17:10,946 --> 00:17:15,659
Actually, our son is getting ready
to take over TS Group.

224
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:17,536
Director Choi Do-yoon?

225
00:17:17,619 --> 00:17:18,454
Yes.

226
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:21,707
If you two help us out this time,

227
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:24,960
I'll return the favor
when you're in a bind.

228
00:17:41,852 --> 00:17:42,811
Sir.

229
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:52,780
Sir.

230
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,198
We have a problem.

231
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:28,148
-He's coming out!
-There he is!

232
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:31,985
-A few words about Mr. Baek Ho-rang?
-Any comment on Mr. Baek?

233
00:18:34,905 --> 00:18:36,949
Do you have anything to say
about Mr. Baek?

234
00:18:37,032 --> 00:18:40,035
As a member of the family,

235
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:44,331
I take full responsibility
for all the controversies surrounding him.

236
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:48,377
I'd like to apologize to the public
on his behalf.

237
00:18:49,711 --> 00:18:52,631
DOSEONG DAILY
"TS HOTEL EXECUTIVE COMES CLEAN"

238
00:18:59,429 --> 00:19:01,849
BAEK HO-RANG BETRAYS FAMILY,
EMBEZZLES 8 BILLION WON

239
00:19:01,932 --> 00:19:04,935
I almost fainted when I read the article.

240
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:06,395
My nephew…

241
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:09,148
My own nephew!

242
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:15,320
Embezzling money from TS Hotel
just to screw Do-yoon and me over?

243
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:18,615
I can't believe it. It's terrible!

244
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:21,827
The media is in a frenzy.

245
00:19:21,910 --> 00:19:24,204
It's all over social media and YouTube.

246
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:25,622
There's even a petition.

247
00:19:25,706 --> 00:19:28,250
This doesn't look like
it'll blow over anytime soon.

248
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:29,459
And the stock's tanked.

249
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:30,836
Is this true, Mr. Baek?

250
00:19:30,919 --> 00:19:33,422
Say something, will you?

251
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,216
Senior Managing Director Baek.

252
00:19:36,717 --> 00:19:38,343
Are you out of your mind?

253
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:41,430
It's true I had a meal
with Vice President Yoon Dong-seok.

254
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:45,058
And it's true we talked
about the embezzlement case.

255
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:46,768
Look at him.

256
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:50,772
That's why you can't trust anyone,
not even your own flesh and blood.

257
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:52,649
That bastard.

258
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:55,444
He thought
he could walk all over TS Group--

259
00:19:55,527 --> 00:19:56,528
Quiet.

260
00:20:00,949 --> 00:20:01,867
And?

261
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:06,872
He met me as a whistleblower
in the TS Hotel embezzlement case.

262
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:08,624
He had evidence.

263
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:10,292
Senior Managing Director Baek!

264
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:11,251
Sit down.

265
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:17,549
Listen, Yoon Dong-seok
already confessed to everything.

266
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:20,761
I heard he gave you the ledgers
on a regular basis.

267
00:20:20,844 --> 00:20:23,222
Where did you hide them?
Where are the ledgers?

268
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:25,432
I can submit the evidence right now.

269
00:20:26,099 --> 00:20:28,727
-Even to the media.
-Some evidence would be nice.

270
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:30,771
If you're innocent, prove it.

271
00:20:31,396 --> 00:20:34,316
Chairwoman, let's trust Ho-rang and wait.

272
00:20:34,399 --> 00:20:36,360
He says he's got evidence and all.

273
00:20:36,443 --> 00:20:38,987
I was just starting to think
you had potential.

274
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:42,741
If you don't fix this,

275
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,619
I'll drop you without a second thought.

276
00:20:45,702 --> 00:20:47,120
You know that, right?

277
00:20:48,956 --> 00:20:51,416
Anyone can be replaced.

278
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:59,258
Maybe you should talk to Seol-hee.

279
00:21:11,603 --> 00:21:13,105
I'll head down first.

280
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:27,286
I guess you got in touch
with my grandmother.

281
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:28,620
Yes.

282
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:31,832
I actually know Yoon Dong-seok.

283
00:21:31,915 --> 00:21:33,667
I met him a few times with Do-yoon.

284
00:21:34,584 --> 00:21:37,504
I know what they often talked about.

285
00:21:37,587 --> 00:21:40,007
I also know Yoon Dong-seok's weaknesses.

286
00:21:40,632 --> 00:21:41,842
And

287
00:21:41,925 --> 00:21:45,178
I know that Yoon Dong-seok is framing you.

288
00:21:48,849 --> 00:21:50,809
You'll be my witness?

289
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:54,396
Not just a witness.

290
00:21:54,896 --> 00:21:57,816
I can use Hanlim's influence to help you.

291
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:01,320
I'm saying I have the card
to turn this around.

292
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:04,698
And I have the means
to get the message out.

293
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:11,288
I assume
you're not offering to do it for free.

294
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:13,915
There has to be a catch.

295
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:16,376
Of course.

296
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:18,712
You know I want something from you.

297
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:24,926
I'll save

298
00:22:26,053 --> 00:22:28,764
both TS and you.

299
00:22:30,724 --> 00:22:32,768
Wouldn't marrying me be

300
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:34,561
a pretty good deal?

301
00:22:37,439 --> 00:22:39,900
Baek Ho-rang,
senior managing director of TS Resort,

302
00:22:39,983 --> 00:22:42,944
is under suspicion
of embezzling funds from TS Hotel.

303
00:22:43,028 --> 00:22:47,949
Backlash against Mr. Baek is growing
as new mistreatment allegations emerge.

304
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:49,951
A close confidant claims

305
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:53,080
Mr. Baek has long suffered
from a serious mental illness.

306
00:22:53,163 --> 00:22:55,957
The crisis has ignited debate
over the company's leadership.

307
00:22:56,041 --> 00:22:59,795
-What is this?
-Similar concerns over its successor…

308
00:23:19,731 --> 00:23:22,651
Guys, I'm on my way to meet
that notorious writer.

309
00:23:22,734 --> 00:23:27,197
Check out this fancy neighborhood.
How much do you have to make to live here?

310
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:28,115
Look at these houses.

311
00:23:28,198 --> 00:23:29,991
Here we are, guys.

312
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:32,577
All right, I'm ringing the bell.

313
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:35,247
RUBBER GLOVE

314
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:47,426
Who is it?

315
00:23:48,135 --> 00:23:50,303
Ms. Na Bo-bae? Delivery.

316
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:52,180
I need your signature.

317
00:23:54,057 --> 00:23:55,183
A delivery?

318
00:23:55,892 --> 00:23:59,855
Guys, this is it.
We're about to meet that troublemaker.

319
00:23:59,938 --> 00:24:03,400
I think she's coming out.
Told you I'd get to the bottom of this.

320
00:24:03,483 --> 00:24:05,360
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

321
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:07,654
I live right across the street.

322
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:10,115
You said delivery. Where's the package?

323
00:24:10,198 --> 00:24:12,451
Mind your own business. Just move along.

324
00:24:13,034 --> 00:24:15,245
-I told you, I live across the street.
-So?

325
00:24:15,328 --> 00:24:18,123
Heard there's a burglar around here.
Was it you?

326
00:24:18,206 --> 00:24:21,293
A burglar? I'm a reporter!
See this camera?

327
00:24:21,877 --> 00:24:24,087
A reporter? Which outlet?

328
00:24:24,171 --> 00:24:26,173
What's it to you?

329
00:24:27,841 --> 00:24:29,759
Why are you covering your face?

330
00:24:29,843 --> 00:24:31,303
You live in a fancy area.

331
00:24:31,386 --> 00:24:33,054
Are you famous or--

332
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:36,558
You tried to hit me with that camera.
You're the burglar.

333
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:39,728
You bastard! I'm gonna call the cops!

334
00:24:39,811 --> 00:24:41,354
Call the cops? Think you can?

335
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:44,566
A fake courier calling the cops
after filming and assaulting someone?

336
00:24:44,649 --> 00:24:46,193
-Be my guest.
-That hurts!

337
00:24:46,276 --> 00:24:47,152
Damn it.

338
00:24:51,114 --> 00:24:53,492
Let me go! You're breaking my arm!

339
00:24:53,575 --> 00:24:56,495
You're gonna break it! Damn it!

340
00:24:56,578 --> 00:24:59,122
Let go, you bastard! This is expensive!

341
00:25:00,665 --> 00:25:01,541
Eun-ho.

342
00:25:09,466 --> 00:25:12,219
How did you know I was here?

343
00:25:17,933 --> 00:25:19,267
I was waiting next door.

344
00:25:19,976 --> 00:25:21,603
I heard what that guy said.

345
00:25:21,686 --> 00:25:23,021
Oh.

346
00:25:28,902 --> 00:25:30,362
I'm sorry I lied to you.

347
00:25:30,445 --> 00:25:33,865
No, I'm sorry
for putting you through this.

348
00:25:38,078 --> 00:25:39,871
Even after I got rejected.

349
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:44,501
I like you, Bo-bae.

350
00:25:52,717 --> 00:25:54,219
The last three years…

351
00:25:55,845 --> 00:25:57,806
I only got through it because of you.

352
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:04,354
There wasn't a single day
you didn't help me, Eun-ho.

353
00:26:06,231 --> 00:26:08,441
You always said you were my fan

354
00:26:09,526 --> 00:26:11,903
and wanted to keep reading my scripts.

355
00:26:14,614 --> 00:26:16,199
That's how I got this far.

356
00:26:19,786 --> 00:26:21,454
Why do I have a bad feeling?

357
00:26:24,874 --> 00:26:25,875
But…

358
00:26:32,257 --> 00:26:34,926
I found someone who feels like fate.

359
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:37,512
And…

360
00:26:39,514 --> 00:26:41,016
it's not you.

361
00:26:44,144 --> 00:26:45,186
I'm sorry.

362
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:01,453
That's just cruel.

363
00:27:02,704 --> 00:27:04,164
I'm sorry, Eun-ho.

364
00:27:17,344 --> 00:27:19,304
How's Mr. Fate doing?

365
00:27:19,804 --> 00:27:21,890
I saw the news.
Looks like it's a real mess.

366
00:27:21,973 --> 00:27:23,099
Oh.

367
00:27:26,269 --> 00:27:27,896
I don't really know.

368
00:27:28,396 --> 00:27:30,106
It's got nothing to do with me.

369
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:32,025
Then why do you look like that?

370
00:27:32,734 --> 00:27:34,235
Lighten up.

371
00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:35,445
Huh?

372
00:27:36,237 --> 00:27:37,238
Right.

373
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:43,119
Try not to worry too much.

374
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:47,874
I don't know Mr. Baek that well,

375
00:27:48,792 --> 00:27:53,588
but he's not the type
to embezzle or mistreat people.

376
00:27:55,632 --> 00:27:56,966
You'd know better than I do.

377
00:28:05,767 --> 00:28:07,811
I'll get going.

378
00:28:09,187 --> 00:28:11,356
Don't open the door to strangers.

379
00:28:11,856 --> 00:28:12,691
Okay.

380
00:28:15,527 --> 00:28:16,486
Bo-bae.

381
00:28:18,780 --> 00:28:21,533
You rejected me,
but I'm still your number one fan.

382
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:24,035
I'll keep rooting for you.

383
00:28:24,119 --> 00:28:25,870
I'm the male lead in your drama.

384
00:28:25,954 --> 00:28:27,706
Seriously…

385
00:28:30,291 --> 00:28:31,334
And

386
00:28:32,877 --> 00:28:34,879
don't let the rumors about us bother you.

387
00:28:36,381 --> 00:28:38,091
Okay. I won't.

388
00:28:39,926 --> 00:28:42,512
No dating. Just write.
Your number one fan's waiting.

389
00:28:43,096 --> 00:28:44,764
Dating? I'm not dating.

390
00:28:45,473 --> 00:28:48,017
Go on. Go act.

391
00:28:48,101 --> 00:28:49,352
I'm your fan too.

392
00:28:49,436 --> 00:28:51,688
Oh, thank you.

393
00:28:53,189 --> 00:28:54,733
I'm off. Don't come out.

394
00:29:11,833 --> 00:29:13,501
You're surprisingly bold.

395
00:29:14,002 --> 00:29:16,212
I didn't expect you
to bring me to a suite.

396
00:29:16,796 --> 00:29:18,423
This is the most secure place.

397
00:29:21,217 --> 00:29:25,430
And I think I'm starting to see
what kind of person you are.

398
00:29:27,390 --> 00:29:28,641
What kind of person am I?

399
00:29:29,976 --> 00:29:31,102
Someone

400
00:29:32,562 --> 00:29:33,521
like me.

401
00:29:39,694 --> 00:29:41,488
Spot on.

402
00:29:42,197 --> 00:29:43,990
I like that answer.

403
00:29:45,658 --> 00:29:48,453
So are you attracted to me now?

404
00:29:49,746 --> 00:29:51,206
Back in Jeju,

405
00:29:51,706 --> 00:29:56,169
you said that having many plans
meant I wasn't certain.

406
00:29:57,003 --> 00:29:59,297
You're right. I'm uncertain and anxious.

407
00:29:59,923 --> 00:30:02,258
Anxious to hide my weaknesses perfectly.

408
00:30:03,009 --> 00:30:03,843
Then…

409
00:30:03,927 --> 00:30:04,928
Even so,

410
00:30:05,011 --> 00:30:08,389
I'll have to decline your offer.

411
00:30:09,224 --> 00:30:13,269
I've lived with anxiety and doubt
my whole life,

412
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:16,773
so I tend to stay calm
in situations like this.

413
00:30:19,567 --> 00:30:22,654
You brought me all the way here
just to tell me that?

414
00:30:22,737 --> 00:30:23,780
Yes.

415
00:30:23,863 --> 00:30:26,115
I'm turning you down once and for all.

416
00:30:26,908 --> 00:30:28,368
If someone saw this,

417
00:30:30,078 --> 00:30:31,496
I figured you'd be embarrassed.

418
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:39,879
You never know.

419
00:30:40,505 --> 00:30:43,258
Someone could be secretly recording this

420
00:30:43,758 --> 00:30:45,176
and editing it

421
00:30:46,010 --> 00:30:47,095
to suit their agenda.

422
00:31:05,905 --> 00:31:10,326
I didn't expect
Director Han Seol-hee to play dirty.

423
00:31:11,202 --> 00:31:13,288
No wonder she's always with Choi Do-yoon.

424
00:31:13,788 --> 00:31:16,749
Did she admit to making up the rumors
about Mr. Ji Eun-ho?

425
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:19,627
She didn't have to. Her face said it all.

426
00:31:19,711 --> 00:31:21,004
Where are the secretaries?

427
00:31:21,087 --> 00:31:22,839
They rushed back to the office.

428
00:31:22,922 --> 00:31:24,591
Oh, I should call Ms. Na too.

429
00:31:24,674 --> 00:31:25,925
No, don't call her.

430
00:31:27,218 --> 00:31:29,137
Sorry? But surely…

431
00:31:31,931 --> 00:31:33,141
I said don't call her.

432
00:31:34,517 --> 00:31:35,351
Yes, sir.

433
00:31:43,359 --> 00:31:45,486
Wow, it's Ji Eun-ho!

434
00:31:50,283 --> 00:31:51,492
Hello.

435
00:31:51,993 --> 00:31:55,246
I'm Kang Du-ri,
director of The Voice of the Night.

436
00:32:06,299 --> 00:32:08,509
Yes, I'm okay.

437
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:11,304
There isn't any reason not to be.

438
00:32:11,387 --> 00:32:14,974
I'm grateful I was given the chance
to make such a fun movie.

439
00:32:15,058 --> 00:32:18,519
Thank you all for coming today.

440
00:32:19,187 --> 00:32:23,566
If I can just say something real quick,
unrelated to the movie…

441
00:32:27,111 --> 00:32:30,239
The woman in the video
that's been going around

442
00:32:30,323 --> 00:32:31,950
is indeed a drama writer.

443
00:32:34,535 --> 00:32:36,204
What's he doing?

444
00:32:36,287 --> 00:32:39,290
But there are stories going around
that aren't true.

445
00:32:39,374 --> 00:32:41,876
That I proposed to her

446
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:44,087
or that she used me.

447
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:47,340
Those are completely untrue.

448
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:55,223
She's simply someone
who works hard at writing her scripts.

449
00:32:55,974 --> 00:32:58,059
She's someone I deeply respect.

450
00:33:04,857 --> 00:33:07,318
I've never had feelings for her
beyond that.

451
00:33:08,736 --> 00:33:10,446
Not once.

452
00:33:12,573 --> 00:33:15,118
That I proposed to her

453
00:33:15,201 --> 00:33:17,328
or that she used me.

454
00:33:17,829 --> 00:33:20,623
-You said not to worry.
-Those are completely untrue.

455
00:33:21,541 --> 00:33:22,667
Liar.

456
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:26,462
She's simply someone who works hard…

457
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:28,464
-What a guy.
-…at writing her scripts.

458
00:33:30,133 --> 00:33:32,260
She's someone I deeply respect.

459
00:33:32,343 --> 00:33:34,303
I've never had feelings for her
beyond that.

460
00:33:35,221 --> 00:33:36,806
Not once.

461
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:42,353
That's a relief.

462
00:33:43,146 --> 00:33:44,772
-I understand.
-That's right.

463
00:33:44,856 --> 00:33:46,607
The reports going around aren't true.

464
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:47,942
They are completely false.

465
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:50,653
I'll take care of it right away. Yes.

466
00:33:50,737 --> 00:33:52,655
Do we have a venue
for the press conference?

467
00:33:52,739 --> 00:33:53,656
Yes.

468
00:33:55,033 --> 00:33:55,867
Here it is.

469
00:33:55,950 --> 00:33:58,077
-Thanks.
-This is TS Resort.

470
00:33:58,161 --> 00:34:00,079
The reports are completely false.

471
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:08,963
12:11 A.M.

472
00:34:34,363 --> 00:34:35,198
Don't you…

473
00:34:37,200 --> 00:34:38,242
need to charge?

474
00:34:39,243 --> 00:34:40,328
Oh.

475
00:34:40,828 --> 00:34:42,038
It's late,

476
00:34:43,456 --> 00:34:47,794
so I was just charging from here,
1% at a time.

477
00:34:50,004 --> 00:34:51,631
You could've asked me.

478
00:34:52,215 --> 00:34:53,800
Charging you is part of our contract.

479
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:26,624
It'll finally be over tomorrow.

480
00:35:28,626 --> 00:35:29,752
The embezzlement case.

481
00:35:30,336 --> 00:35:32,255
We're holding a press conference.

482
00:35:33,005 --> 00:35:33,923
Right.

483
00:35:34,924 --> 00:35:35,967
That's good.

484
00:35:36,717 --> 00:35:41,764
But a press conference means
you'll be surrounded by cameras.

485
00:35:42,723 --> 00:35:45,059
It's the quickest and easiest way.

486
00:35:46,686 --> 00:35:49,814
If I take my meds and stay calm,

487
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:52,650
I think I'll manage.

488
00:35:52,733 --> 00:35:55,611
But what if you start panicking again?

489
00:35:57,321 --> 00:35:59,532
You can't risk that
in front of the cameras.

490
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:02,827
Yeah, I can't.

491
00:36:04,203 --> 00:36:05,371
But it's okay.

492
00:36:06,956 --> 00:36:08,207
I'm sure I'll be fine.

493
00:36:11,043 --> 00:36:14,088
I have to do a good job.

494
00:36:17,133 --> 00:36:19,802
That's the only way I can take over TS.

495
00:36:20,636 --> 00:36:22,430
But why go that far?

496
00:36:25,349 --> 00:36:27,018
Because of my parents.

497
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:32,398
I know what kind of company

498
00:36:32,481 --> 00:36:35,568
my parents wanted TS to be.

499
00:36:36,694 --> 00:36:40,031
I'm the only one who can do it.

500
00:36:42,491 --> 00:36:45,369
It's something I have to see through.

501
00:36:47,788 --> 00:36:48,998
To do so,

502
00:36:49,081 --> 00:36:51,042
I'll have to overcome…

503
00:36:54,128 --> 00:36:55,838
the cameras and the flashes.

504
00:36:59,091 --> 00:37:02,720
Why are you so afraid of cameras?

505
00:37:07,558 --> 00:37:08,434
I'm not sure.

506
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:12,355
To be more precise…

507
00:37:14,607 --> 00:37:16,692
I'm afraid

508
00:37:18,611 --> 00:37:19,654
of people's eyes

509
00:37:20,988 --> 00:37:22,240
on me.

510
00:37:23,115 --> 00:37:24,200
He's here!

511
00:37:24,283 --> 00:37:25,201
It's Ho-rang!

512
00:37:25,284 --> 00:37:26,744
-It's Ho-rang.
-Ho-rang!

513
00:37:27,745 --> 00:37:29,205
Ho-rang!

514
00:37:29,288 --> 00:37:30,289
Ho-rang!

515
00:37:31,082 --> 00:37:32,291
Look this way, Ho-rang!

516
00:37:32,375 --> 00:37:34,502
Look here, Ho-rang!

517
00:37:34,585 --> 00:37:36,003
Just one interview!

518
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,927
Ho-rang! Just one interview!

519
00:37:43,010 --> 00:37:44,053
Ho-rang!

520
00:37:50,309 --> 00:37:53,104
Ho-rang, don't you feel bad
for your parents?

521
00:38:04,865 --> 00:38:08,202
I told you last time.

522
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:11,831
When my parents died in an accident
because of me…

523
00:38:11,914 --> 00:38:14,166
How was it your fault?

524
00:38:15,501 --> 00:38:18,921
An accident is just an accident.

525
00:38:19,005 --> 00:38:21,299
It happened
because they were coming to see me.

526
00:38:21,382 --> 00:38:23,384
Of course they were. They're your parents.

527
00:38:23,467 --> 00:38:25,636
That's what parents do. It's love.

528
00:38:26,220 --> 00:38:29,682
The people who shoved cameras in your face
were in the wrong.

529
00:38:29,765 --> 00:38:32,393
Why should you feel bad?
How is it your fault?

530
00:38:42,486 --> 00:38:43,404
Well…

531
00:38:45,740 --> 00:38:46,824
I guess you're right.

532
00:38:56,042 --> 00:38:57,168
Look at me.

533
00:38:59,128 --> 00:39:00,546
I know

534
00:39:01,339 --> 00:39:03,257
what kind of person Baek Ho-rang is.

535
00:39:04,467 --> 00:39:07,345
On the outside,
the perfect senior managing director,

536
00:39:08,179 --> 00:39:11,182
always sticking to the plan.

537
00:39:11,891 --> 00:39:13,225
But underneath,

538
00:39:13,809 --> 00:39:15,394
full of worries,

539
00:39:16,729 --> 00:39:18,314
always anxious,

540
00:39:19,523 --> 00:39:23,235
always taking care of other people
before himself…

541
00:39:26,572 --> 00:39:28,324
That's how kind you are.

542
00:39:34,538 --> 00:39:36,624
Professor Jang told me this.

543
00:39:38,167 --> 00:39:39,502
Sometimes in life,

544
00:39:39,585 --> 00:39:42,380
even a strange little straw

545
00:39:43,089 --> 00:39:45,049
can save a life.

546
00:39:45,132 --> 00:39:46,926
Just one straw.

547
00:39:47,718 --> 00:39:50,388
So all you need is one.

548
00:39:50,471 --> 00:39:52,139
Just one person.

549
00:39:53,682 --> 00:39:56,477
Someone who sees you for who you are.

550
00:39:58,396 --> 00:39:59,522
You're right.

551
00:40:01,982 --> 00:40:02,817
Just one…

552
00:40:06,028 --> 00:40:07,571
Just one person is enough.

553
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:12,159
So don't worry about anyone else.

554
00:40:13,786 --> 00:40:16,872
Just imagine all the eyes
behind the cameras are mine.

555
00:40:17,706 --> 00:40:20,543
Looking at you

556
00:40:20,626 --> 00:40:22,711
like this.

557
00:40:34,390 --> 00:40:35,391
Well…

558
00:40:37,601 --> 00:40:40,563
I meant every word I said,

559
00:40:40,646 --> 00:40:44,400
but it was only out of human kindness.

560
00:40:44,483 --> 00:40:47,611
You know, out of compassion.

561
00:40:48,446 --> 00:40:50,197
And because of our contract.

562
00:40:51,115 --> 00:40:52,116
I understand.

563
00:40:54,201 --> 00:40:55,077
But still,

564
00:40:56,078 --> 00:41:00,249
if you came with me tomorrow…

565
00:41:05,045 --> 00:41:07,423
I think I'd do better.

566
00:41:18,017 --> 00:41:19,602
We're not exactly in a position

567
00:41:20,561 --> 00:41:24,023
to attend an official event together.

568
00:41:24,607 --> 00:41:25,691
You'll do fine.

569
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:28,110
Just remember what I told you.

570
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:31,697
Okay.

571
00:41:35,868 --> 00:41:37,203
I'll get going now.

572
00:41:56,472 --> 00:41:58,641
Stay strong, Na Bo-bae.

573
00:42:00,935 --> 00:42:03,103
Don't feel sorry for him.

574
00:42:06,649 --> 00:42:10,069
Stop thinking about it.

575
00:42:20,996 --> 00:42:22,456
SEO-JEONG

576
00:42:29,421 --> 00:42:33,050
Hey, Na Bo-bae.

577
00:42:33,133 --> 00:42:34,677
-Did you order already?
-Yeah.

578
00:42:35,177 --> 00:42:36,929
Let me pour you a drink.

579
00:42:37,680 --> 00:42:38,639
Oh dear.

580
00:42:38,722 --> 00:42:41,267
Hey, at least Eun-ho's loyal, huh?

581
00:42:41,350 --> 00:42:44,353
He dropped it live at the premiere.

582
00:42:44,436 --> 00:42:46,188
He went all in defending you.

583
00:42:46,272 --> 00:42:47,398
Yeah, he did.

584
00:42:48,065 --> 00:42:51,151
Then why the long face?
The rumor's all cleared up.

585
00:42:51,235 --> 00:42:53,654
What long face?
I'm in a good mood. Cheers.

586
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:59,118
You sure about that?

587
00:42:59,868 --> 00:43:02,705
Don't tell me
it's because of Baek Ho-rang.

588
00:43:02,788 --> 00:43:04,832
-Because of his embezzlement?
-Hey.

589
00:43:06,333 --> 00:43:09,086
You really think he embezzled money?
He has no reason to.

590
00:43:09,169 --> 00:43:10,421
Look at you.

591
00:43:11,297 --> 00:43:13,299
What are you, his lawyer?

592
00:43:18,596 --> 00:43:20,472
You like Baek Ho-rang, don't you?

593
00:43:22,182 --> 00:43:23,142
What?

594
00:43:23,225 --> 00:43:24,226
What…

595
00:43:25,477 --> 00:43:28,439
What are you talking about? Why would I…

596
00:43:28,522 --> 00:43:30,024
That overreaction says it all.

597
00:43:30,107 --> 00:43:31,984
Who are you trying to fool?

598
00:43:32,067 --> 00:43:34,028
I had a feeling ever since Jeju.

599
00:43:34,111 --> 00:43:36,447
I'm Cho Seo-jeong. Relationship expert.

600
00:43:36,530 --> 00:43:37,489
Your story bag.

601
00:43:37,573 --> 00:43:39,366
I said I don't like him.

602
00:43:41,118 --> 00:43:43,412
We'll be done
once the contract's over anyway.

603
00:43:44,913 --> 00:43:46,915
He'll just keep getting hurt
if he's with me.

604
00:43:46,999 --> 00:43:47,833
Look at you.

605
00:43:47,916 --> 00:43:50,336
There you go,
digging yourself into a hole again.

606
00:43:50,919 --> 00:43:53,297
Look, even after the contract's over,

607
00:43:53,380 --> 00:43:55,341
you can still see each other.

608
00:43:55,424 --> 00:43:56,425
And him getting hurt?

609
00:43:56,508 --> 00:43:58,260
Your powers don't even work on him.

610
00:43:58,344 --> 00:44:00,262
Maybe not directly,

611
00:44:00,929 --> 00:44:03,307
but he got hurt because of me
at the airport.

612
00:44:03,807 --> 00:44:06,018
He probably already knows about my powers.

613
00:44:06,935 --> 00:44:08,103
Did you ask him?

614
00:44:08,854 --> 00:44:09,688
About what?

615
00:44:09,772 --> 00:44:12,483
You did the same thing to me
in high school.

616
00:44:20,282 --> 00:44:21,116
Move.

617
00:44:38,759 --> 00:44:40,511
Cho Seo-jeong…

618
00:44:42,888 --> 00:44:44,848
Don't let those losers get you down.

619
00:44:47,226 --> 00:44:48,602
You saw it too.

620
00:44:50,396 --> 00:44:51,522
I hurt his hand, and--

621
00:44:51,605 --> 00:44:53,732
Oh please, he barely got hurt.

622
00:44:53,816 --> 00:44:55,192
He was being dramatic.

623
00:44:55,776 --> 00:44:57,611
Why does that even matter?

624
00:44:57,695 --> 00:44:59,488
I'm your friend.

625
00:45:00,531 --> 00:45:02,032
I'll always be on your side.

626
00:45:08,539 --> 00:45:09,748
That's all that matters.

627
00:45:23,512 --> 00:45:25,556
What if I hadn't put on
rubber gloves that day?

628
00:45:25,639 --> 00:45:26,932
You would've been like,

629
00:45:27,433 --> 00:45:30,269
"Cho Seo-jeong's just like everyone else."

630
00:45:32,020 --> 00:45:34,022
You would've run away from me.

631
00:45:34,106 --> 00:45:36,608
No, that's different from this.

632
00:45:36,692 --> 00:45:38,694
You keep doing it.

633
00:45:39,194 --> 00:45:41,113
I'm seeing a pattern here.

634
00:45:41,613 --> 00:45:43,198
That's your problem, damn it!

635
00:45:43,907 --> 00:45:45,701
I'm sorry.

636
00:45:45,784 --> 00:45:46,952
That's your problem.

637
00:45:47,035 --> 00:45:49,455
You're always hung up
on that electricity thing.

638
00:45:49,538 --> 00:45:50,831
You get scared and run away.

639
00:45:50,914 --> 00:45:52,791
Wouldn't you do the same?

640
00:45:52,875 --> 00:45:55,169
Do you know how hard it is
to live like this?

641
00:45:55,669 --> 00:45:56,628
No, I don't.

642
00:45:56,712 --> 00:45:58,338
But I do know one thing.

643
00:45:58,422 --> 00:46:01,049
You're just a coward
putting on a tough front.

644
00:46:01,133 --> 00:46:03,552
Like the rumors with Ji Eun-ho.

645
00:46:03,635 --> 00:46:05,721
You just let everyone witch-hunt you.

646
00:46:05,804 --> 00:46:09,057
If I were you,
I'd make a statement or sue them.

647
00:46:09,141 --> 00:46:11,810
How can you just sit there and take it?

648
00:46:15,606 --> 00:46:17,900
If it weren't for Ji Eun-ho,

649
00:46:17,983 --> 00:46:20,444
you'd be finished, Bo-bae.

650
00:46:20,944 --> 00:46:22,488
-Stop already.
-Stop what?

651
00:46:23,447 --> 00:46:25,491
Is there anyone else who tells you this?

652
00:46:25,574 --> 00:46:26,617
No, there isn't.

653
00:46:26,700 --> 00:46:27,951
I said stop already!

654
00:46:35,167 --> 00:46:37,753
Truth hurts, huh?
You're mad 'cause I'm right.

655
00:46:37,836 --> 00:46:40,422
How old are you? Act your age.

656
00:46:40,506 --> 00:46:42,591
Right back at you!

657
00:46:42,674 --> 00:46:44,259
Jeez.

658
00:46:47,679 --> 00:46:48,514
So?

659
00:46:49,723 --> 00:46:51,934
You gonna get all scared
and run away again?

660
00:47:15,332 --> 00:47:17,584
Sir, are you sure you'll be okay?

661
00:47:21,380 --> 00:47:23,757
I thought so. You don't look well.

662
00:47:36,270 --> 00:47:37,312
I'm fine.

663
00:47:48,031 --> 00:47:49,616
It's Senior Managing Director Baek.

664
00:48:15,142 --> 00:48:16,685
Why did you embezzle the money?

665
00:48:18,645 --> 00:48:21,064
BAEK HO-RANG
EMERGENCY PRESS CONFERENCE

666
00:48:21,148 --> 00:48:23,525
-Please move aside.
-Please sit down.

667
00:48:23,609 --> 00:48:24,443
Take a seat.

668
00:48:45,589 --> 00:48:47,507
So don't worry about anyone else.

669
00:48:48,091 --> 00:48:51,136
Just imagine all the eyes
behind the cameras are mine.

670
00:48:51,970 --> 00:48:54,806
Looking at you

671
00:48:55,390 --> 00:48:56,934
like this.

672
00:49:36,640 --> 00:49:41,353
I'd like to make a statement

673
00:49:42,562 --> 00:49:45,607
regarding the recent
embezzlement case at TS Hotel.

674
00:49:51,321 --> 00:49:57,411
I have never embezzled a single cent
from TS Hotel.

675
00:49:58,286 --> 00:50:00,497
I'll fully cooperate with the police

676
00:50:00,580 --> 00:50:04,001
to ensure the real culprit

677
00:50:05,794 --> 00:50:07,045
is brought to justice.

678
00:50:23,520 --> 00:50:25,147
Move out of the way.

679
00:50:25,230 --> 00:50:26,690
I can't see!

680
00:50:26,773 --> 00:50:29,484
I'm Yoon Dong-seok,
the one who named Mr. Baek Ho-rang

681
00:50:29,985 --> 00:50:31,194
as an accomplice.

682
00:50:32,029 --> 00:50:34,239
My real accomplice…

683
00:50:38,285 --> 00:50:40,495
is Assemblyman Choi Tae-sik.

684
00:50:41,455 --> 00:50:42,581
I'm sorry.

685
00:50:42,664 --> 00:50:45,375
What's that crazy bastard saying?

686
00:50:45,459 --> 00:50:47,335
That crazy bastard.

687
00:50:47,419 --> 00:50:49,379
Where's Choi Do-yoon?

688
00:50:49,463 --> 00:50:51,590
He said he took care of it!

689
00:50:51,673 --> 00:50:55,677
We paid off Doseong Daily and JBS.
What the hell's going on?

690
00:50:55,761 --> 00:50:57,095
Call them! Now!

691
00:50:59,139 --> 00:50:59,973
Damn it.

692
00:51:01,224 --> 00:51:02,059
I'm sorry.

693
00:51:02,893 --> 00:51:03,727
Gyeong-jin?

694
00:51:03,810 --> 00:51:05,812
Baek Gyeong-jin!

695
00:51:05,896 --> 00:51:06,897
Hey, call 911!

696
00:51:06,980 --> 00:51:09,775
Wake up, Gyeong-jin. Baek Gyeong-jin!

697
00:51:11,359 --> 00:51:12,319
Are you saying

698
00:51:12,402 --> 00:51:17,324
you'll let TS Hotel
publish false articles?

699
00:51:20,243 --> 00:51:22,120
It might be better that way.

700
00:51:22,204 --> 00:51:24,206
Once they let their guard down,

701
00:51:24,289 --> 00:51:25,415
we can do

702
00:51:26,124 --> 00:51:27,793
what we have to do.

703
00:51:32,756 --> 00:51:34,216
What the hell? Who are you?

704
00:51:34,299 --> 00:51:36,593
Let go!

705
00:51:41,473 --> 00:51:42,599
Baek…

706
00:51:42,682 --> 00:51:44,059
Mr. Baek.

707
00:51:48,188 --> 00:51:49,481
What is going on?

708
00:51:54,402 --> 00:51:55,695
Mr. Yoon.

709
00:51:56,196 --> 00:51:58,406
Did you really think I wouldn't know?

710
00:51:59,324 --> 00:52:00,367
Sorry?

711
00:52:00,450 --> 00:52:04,454
You thought you could frame me
with a fake ledger.

712
00:52:05,205 --> 00:52:06,998
I'm not that sloppy.

713
00:52:08,291 --> 00:52:09,709
Fake? This is real.

714
00:52:09,793 --> 00:52:13,588
I already have ten years
of slush fund transfer records.

715
00:52:19,636 --> 00:52:20,679
Let me guess.

716
00:52:20,762 --> 00:52:23,014
My aunt and uncle promised

717
00:52:23,515 --> 00:52:26,143
you'd be set for life
if you did some time?

718
00:52:26,226 --> 00:52:28,311
Or was it Choi Do-yoon?

719
00:52:29,855 --> 00:52:30,689
It's just--

720
00:52:30,772 --> 00:52:32,190
Do you trust them?

721
00:52:32,858 --> 00:52:33,984
Sorry?

722
00:52:34,067 --> 00:52:37,237
I know you did it
for your wife and daughter.

723
00:52:43,493 --> 00:52:44,369
But

724
00:52:45,495 --> 00:52:46,830
is this really

725
00:52:47,914 --> 00:52:49,791
what's best for your family?

726
00:52:49,875 --> 00:52:51,585
Then what should I do?

727
00:52:52,085 --> 00:52:54,045
I did embezzle the money with them.

728
00:52:54,629 --> 00:52:55,922
There's no way out.

729
00:52:56,006 --> 00:52:57,007
Just

730
00:52:57,507 --> 00:52:59,509
do what you have to do.

731
00:52:59,593 --> 00:53:03,138
Pay for your crimes and tell the truth.

732
00:53:04,764 --> 00:53:08,101
Just report Choi Tae-sik first.

733
00:53:10,478 --> 00:53:12,189
I'll take care of the rest.

734
00:53:14,024 --> 00:53:19,279
Mr. Yoon Dong-seok will cooperate
with the police in good faith.

735
00:53:20,405 --> 00:53:25,410
I already have evidence
of the real embezzlement.

736
00:53:26,077 --> 00:53:30,790
I turned it all over
to the police yesterday.

737
00:53:33,460 --> 00:53:38,340
Actor Ji Eun-ho,
who was the victim of malicious rumors,

738
00:53:39,925 --> 00:53:42,761
will continue to be

739
00:53:43,470 --> 00:53:46,097
the face of TS Resort.

740
00:53:47,265 --> 00:53:48,225
Lastly…

741
00:53:51,019 --> 00:53:53,730
to Director Han Seol-hee
of Hanlim Advertising Company,

742
00:53:53,813 --> 00:53:58,401
whose name has been linked to mine
since I was named an accomplice,

743
00:53:59,486 --> 00:54:02,447
I'd like to officially apologize.

744
00:54:03,406 --> 00:54:07,118
For dragging her into false reports
that we were getting married…

745
00:54:09,537 --> 00:54:12,457
I sincerely apologize.

746
00:54:16,795 --> 00:54:19,214
What is your relationship with Ms. Han?

747
00:54:45,824 --> 00:54:47,242
Ms. Na Bo-bae!

748
00:55:06,761 --> 00:55:08,096
You scared me.

749
00:55:08,596 --> 00:55:09,514
Oh, I'm sorry.

750
00:55:11,975 --> 00:55:13,852
How did you…

751
00:55:14,644 --> 00:55:16,229
How did you get here so fast?

752
00:55:18,440 --> 00:55:20,358
There's a shortcut.

753
00:55:38,043 --> 00:55:39,085
But

754
00:55:39,669 --> 00:55:41,171
why did you run away?

755
00:55:42,255 --> 00:55:43,298
I just…

756
00:55:44,966 --> 00:55:49,512
When did I run away? I was just… running.

757
00:55:49,596 --> 00:55:51,222
You ran away when you saw me.

758
00:55:51,306 --> 00:55:52,807
Me? When?

759
00:55:52,891 --> 00:55:55,018
You've been running away…

760
00:55:57,479 --> 00:55:58,688
ever since Jeju.

761
00:56:07,280 --> 00:56:08,156
Ms. Na.

762
00:56:10,241 --> 00:56:11,493
Do you really think…

763
00:56:14,120 --> 00:56:16,664
I don't know anything about you?

764
00:56:18,750 --> 00:56:19,584
What?

765
00:56:20,085 --> 00:56:22,712
Ever since you moved into my house,

766
00:56:23,213 --> 00:56:26,299
we've had blackouts and broken appliances.

767
00:56:27,801 --> 00:56:30,303
And you'd put on rubber gloves
for no reason.

768
00:56:30,845 --> 00:56:33,681
You even called me a human rubber glove.

769
00:56:42,899 --> 00:56:43,983
All this time…

770
00:56:47,695 --> 00:56:49,280
you knew?

771
00:56:50,824 --> 00:56:53,034
I thought it was strange.

772
00:56:54,536 --> 00:56:55,453
But

773
00:56:56,454 --> 00:56:58,498
you didn't seem to want to talk about it,

774
00:56:59,499 --> 00:57:00,500
so I didn't ask.

775
00:57:05,004 --> 00:57:05,964
And

776
00:57:07,841 --> 00:57:09,217
after Jeju…

777
00:57:14,681 --> 00:57:15,682
none of that

778
00:57:17,058 --> 00:57:17,892
mattered

779
00:57:19,102 --> 00:57:20,103
anymore.

780
00:57:22,021 --> 00:57:23,189
Because I like you.

781
00:57:26,776 --> 00:57:27,861
I like you,

782
00:57:29,654 --> 00:57:30,780
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

783
00:57:35,118 --> 00:57:37,454
The electricity, the contract, whatever.

784
00:57:37,537 --> 00:57:38,621
None of it matters.

785
00:57:40,999 --> 00:57:42,208
I just…

786
00:57:44,752 --> 00:57:46,087
like you.

787
00:57:57,557 --> 00:57:58,725
Na Bo-bae is…

788
00:58:02,020 --> 00:58:03,605
just Na Bo-bae.

789
00:58:06,357 --> 00:58:07,525
So

790
00:58:09,277 --> 00:58:11,237
even if I get hurt because of you,

791
00:58:11,863 --> 00:58:13,364
I don't care.

792
01:01:20,677 --> 01:01:25,306
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
